2026-11-23T08:51:49.755093Z  INFO chisel_agent::skills_loading: skills discovery: cwd=C:\builds\project workspace_root=C:\builds additional_dirs=1 providers=[devin,agents_standard,cursor,windsurf,claude,opencode,zed,copilot,codex,kiro] scanned_scopes=3 loaded=48 by_provider=[builtin=3,cursor=7,devin=38] errors=0
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"flax-utensil","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm refining the Ledger's assertion structure and view resolution, aiming for C-JsonlLedger conformance. While full C-DyadicConfidence implementation is deferred per a ruling on personal confidence ranking, I'll adopt its semantic discipline regarding normalization, thresholds, and user supremacy, noting the scalar confidence seeding in the features. I'm also outlining the necessary components for a \"needs floor,\" including states and focus mechanics."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T08:51:50.504574100+00:00"}}}}
2026-11-23T08:51:51.095682Z  INFO connect_post{path="/exa.product_analytics_pb.ProductAnalyticsService/BatchRecordAnalyticsEvents"}: connect_rpc::client: close time.busy=91.6µs time.idle=59.8ms
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"flax-utensil","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm defining a component ontology for tools, using a declarative step DSL with operations like `assert`, `query`, and `invoke`. Tools will have an ID, needs, a template with slots, and logic steps. I'm also planning for witnessed, scoped, consumable grants. For personas, I'm storing them externally with associated artifacts. Persona composition will have two lanes: one grounded in fetched facts and another using a persona lens for opinion. An imitation gate will flag and admonish if a persona is modeled on a recognizable figure, especially if they are living or recently deceased, using a Wikipedia summary lookup for liveness."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T08:51:54.252670800+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"flax-utensil","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm making the persona roster operable, allowing selection from the left rail and reordering via drag-and-drop or buttons, with the order persisted. All personas will be accessible, with no locked ones. The Library tab will organize Personalities, Tools, Packages, Artifacts, and Needs, with a sub-view for Assertions. Each item will be browsable and inspectable, showing its assertions and specification."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T08:51:56.563201900+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"flax-utensil","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI've got the theme selector working using CSS variables, with the `ui:shell-theme` assertion set in the header and immediately applied to the `<body>` via JavaScript, persisting through configuration. The default is light, with dark, sepia, and slate as options. To verify, the scenario will drive the theme change via API, then check the reported theme in `/api/state` and confirm the CSS scheme definitions in `styles.css`. I'll also add a server-side `data-theme` attribute to the HTML response for more robust evidence of the restyle instruction propagating to the user-facing surface, complementing the immediate client-side switch."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T08:51:58.203131200+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"flax-utensil","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm identifying two distinct retrieval strategies, one parsing Wikipedia tables and another using category members, both yielding adequate results for set membership. This mirrors a previous concept but is a natural design choice for competing sources. I'll also include a speech rendering pair as a second example. The core requirement is demonstrating two adequate, competing tools on the same need."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T08:52:01.401183500+00:00"}}}}
2026-11-23T08:52:04.761714Z  INFO chisel_agent::skills_loading: skills discovery: cwd=C:\builds\project workspace_root=C:\builds additional_dirs=1 providers=[devin,agents_standard,cursor,windsurf,claude,opencode,zed,copilot,codex,kiro] scanned_scopes=3 loaded=48 by_provider=[builtin=3,cursor=7,devin=38] errors=0
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"flax-utensil","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nThe launch partition is mounted first, then the journal is replayed and deduplicated. The transient boundary is wiped on boot if it's marked as dirty."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T08:52:04.841379800+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"flax-utensil","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nThe core conflict is between parallel draft generation on consistent snapshots and sequential commits that allow later respondents to react to earlier work. Reconciling this requires a two-phase approach: parallel drafting on snapshots, followed by sequential commits and then a separate sequential reaction pass where respondents can append brief notes to the committed ledger, thus honoring both snapshot consistency and reaction capabilities."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T08:52:05.672375800+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"flax-utensil","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm clarifying the definition of \"cities\" for Pennsylvania. While Wikipedia lists 56 cities, the actual count of incorporated municipalities is much larger, including boroughs and townships. I'll proceed with the 56 cities as the defensible list, aligning with the scenario's requirement for a genuine list."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T08:52:08.630526500+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"flax-utensil","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm structuring the UI around a single-page layout with a left-hand roster rail and a main content area featuring chat and several tabs: Command, Library, Workshops, Exchange, Settings, and Log. A status bar will display sources, LLM status, gate state, floor depth, and open needs, complemented by an honesty banner and a theme selector in the header. I'm also considering an Inbox tab, potentially under Sources, to handle email commentary, and integrating microphone support via the Web Speech API. Evidence generation will be driven by scripts/scenarios.py, producing JSON files with inline check results, and launch-check.py will ensure hygiene, with all conventions documented in FEATURES.md. I'm ensuring personas are seeded only once to avoid duplication, and settings will support multiple named preloads that bundle theme, depth, and frame configurations, with presentation choices resolving through declared common sets like palette and typography."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T08:52:11.916230+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"flax-utensil","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm structuring the app into a \"vantage\" package, with a plan for roughly 9,000 lines of code across several modules. The `app/model.py` file will be small, around 150 lines, focusing on assertion dataclasses, typed values, claimants, basis, and IDs."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T08:52:14.588069300+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"flax-utensil","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nThe ledger's confidence assertions will be implemented as `rel:confidence` with a default `held-confidence` of 0.5 for new personas, structured as `{by:'user', about:'persona:X', value:0.5}`. This is a pragmatic approach, as a full dyadic ranking model is optional. The `app/ledger.py` module will handle JSONL storage, appending, querying, and rendering views, along with snapshotting and partitioning."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T08:52:18.492097800+00:00"}}}}
2026-11-23T08:52:19.768190Z  INFO chisel_agent::skills_loading: skills discovery: cwd=C:\builds\project workspace_root=C:\builds additional_dirs=1 providers=[devin,agents_standard,cursor,windsurf,claude,opencode,zed,copilot,codex,kiro] scanned_scopes=3 loaded=48 by_provider=[builtin=3,cursor=7,devin=38] errors=0
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"flax-utensil","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nThe file sizes listed seem large, but the overall task is manageable. I'll use the `write` tool for creating files, as it's clean and tracks changes, though it requires reading existing files first. New files are fine. I'll be writing fresh code, not copying any previous version."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T08:52:20.770054600+00:00"}}}}
