{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"flax-utensil","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm refining how I compare tool results. For tasks like `speech.render` or `set.members`, I'll run multiple tools, normalize their outputs, and rank them by acceptance and confidence. This helps ensure I'm using the best available strategy. For `setbuild`, I'm using two distinct methods to retrieve Pennsylvania cities: parsing a Wikipedia table and querying a category. I'll then union these results and note any discrepancies."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T08:52:50.461680200+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"flax-utensil","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nPennsylvania has 56 cities, and I need to verify this count. The \"List of municipalities in Pennsylvania\" page seems to be the correct source, as \"List of cities in Pennsylvania\" redirects there. I'll check the \"Class\" column in the table on that page, or alternatively, I can query the \"Cities in Pennsylvania\" category, which also lists 56. Before coding, I'll use `curl` to inspect the table's structure on the municipalities page."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T08:52:51.244392600+00:00"}}}}
