{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"flax-utensil","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"I'm reviewing the `Ctx` object and `builtins.py` for `host.py`, which wires everything together. For `route_input`, I'm mapping chat intents to specific needs: \"set topic\" to `set-topic`, project/list commands to their respective needs, \"create persona\" to `mint`, \"remember\" to `assertion`, and factual questions to `factual-question` for Wikipedia retrieval. Otherwise, it defaults to a conversational response. Intent detection uses simple regex packs, mapping each to a `tool-request` need and a `response` need for conversational replies. The chat turn flow involves input assertion, focus checks, draining servable needs, and then snapshot inference for responses, followed by archiving the turn."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T08:57:26.774553900+00:00"}}}}
