{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"flax-utensil","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm reviewing the `builtins.py` module, specifically the tool definitions. It appears `publish-milestone` requires `publish.artifact` and will refuse if it's missing, while `send-mail` writes to a local outbox and also requires `mail.send`. `set-response-depth` has a required `depth` slot, defaulting to \"3\" if not provided by the user."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T08:57:56.001232400+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"flax-utensil","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm refining the command structure, deciding to use an object.verb format for system commands like `roster.select` and `theme.set`. I'm also considering how to handle speech transcription, mapping browser transcripts to a device witness and then to the turn. For chat responses, I'm evaluating a scoring model for persona selection, balancing confidence, activity, and mention frequency, while ensuring a minimum response depth."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T08:57:58.995783600+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"flax-utensil","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm refining the respondent selection process. The decision model uses a bounded feature vector and weights, with features like `isActive`, `heldConf`, `interestOverlap`, `mentioned`, and `rosterRankNorm`. The weights are configurable, defaulting to `[0.35, 0.4, 0.25, 1.0, 0.1]`, and the score is a weighted sum. This score, along with the selected respondent, is recorded. I'm also clarifying the drafting and committing process: respondents draft in parallel based on personas and a snapshot view, then commit sequentially in ranked order. Subsequent respondents can react to the first committed reply, honoring the C-SequentialRespondents constraint."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T08:58:01.852067800+00:00"}}}}
