{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"flax-utensil","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm refining how `create-project` handles needs. It currently opens a \"generic\" need for candidate ranking, but I'll adjust it to open a \"deliverable\" need, similar to how a goal like \"survey atlases\" would open a \"produce survey\" need with a missing \"format\" slot. This aligns with goals decomposing into tool work. I'm also clarifying intent parsing patterns, mapping phrases like \"set topic to X\" to `set-topic` and \"create project X\" to `create-project`. For factual questions, I'll use a `run-search` need."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T08:58:05.650739100+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"flax-utensil","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm refining how `open_need` handles project goals. Instead of a generic need, I'll use a pseudo-tool `{\"id\":\"project-goal\",\"kind\":\"generic\",\"template\":{\"slots\":[{\"name\":\"format\",\"required\":True}]}}` which will be marked fulfilled with the chosen format, recording it as a `project:deliverable`. This also means goals missing a \"format\" will correctly be deferred as open needs. I'll now write the `builtins.py` file compactly."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T08:58:07.280703800+00:00"}}}}
