{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"flax-utensil","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"It seems all my files are double-spaced, which breaks backslash line continuations. Removing all blank lines is an option, but I need to be careful. Blank lines inside triple-quoted strings are meaningful for content, though removing them is syntactically harmless. However, removing all empty lines could also affect multi-line string literals that don't use literal newlines."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T09:01:52.260902900+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"flax-utensil","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nThe simplest fix is a script that removes an empty line only when the previous non-empty line ends with a backslash. This addresses continuation errors while preserving formatting. I need to check if there are other artifacts, as the double-spacing elsewhere is cosmetic, but `ast.parse` fails only at those five spots. So, the fix is to delete blank lines directly following a line ending in a backslash, then recompile across all `app/*.py` files."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T09:01:52.853586900+00:00"}}}}
