{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"flax-utensil","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI can remove blank lines following backslash-continued lines to fix syntax errors, though this leaves cosmetic double-spacing. A cleaner approach is to strip all blank lines, which deterministically reconstructs the original file density. I must be careful, however, to avoid corrupting triple-quoted strings and to ensure backslash continuations still work after de-spacing. I also noted a potential character corruption (`—` to ``) in `host.py` that seems harmless within string literals."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T09:02:07.883148200+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"flax-utensil","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm checking if removing all blank lines will break multi-line strings in docstrings or literals. So far, it seems okay, as embedded newlines aren't present in strings within the files I've examined. However, a better approach might be to collapse pairs of blank lines into one and single blank lines into none, as the platform seems to insert blanks uniformly."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T09:02:10.567009400+00:00"}}}}
