{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"flax-utensil","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm reviewing the scenario checks, noting that `S-chat-invocation` requires distinguishing tool use from direct replies, and `S-focused-need` defers a response depth setting. `S-personality-roster` and `S-portrait-bind` seem to cover UI elements for personas, while `S-color-schemes` tests theme switching. `S-status-bar` and `S-email-commentary` relate to UI state and interaction feedback. `S-conversation-reset` and `S-context-display` handle state management and UI cues. `S-personality-editor` covers persona modification, and `S-windows-launch` and `S-close-terminate` focus on process management and termination, with the latter requiring a specific enactment."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T09:04:53.419057+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"flax-utensil","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm checking the speech serialization logic: ensuring playback times are sequential and don't overlap, and that distinct replies are generated for similar prompts from multiple personas. I also need to verify that the API holdings section is populated and the UI navigation is present, and that spoken replies accurately reflect factual questions and maintain the correct persona style without inventing information. The driver structure seems fine, and the LLM call latency is acceptable. The speech floor default of 2 responses per scenario should keep run times manageable."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T09:04:58.629193300+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"flax-utensil","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm refining the `S-close-terminate` scenario. The watchdog requires `window_seen` to be true, meaning the SSE connection must have been established at least once. My plan to open, then close the SSE connection before waiting for process exit should satisfy this. I'm also considering reducing the SSE tick interval from 25s to speed up detection, but will leave it for now as the scenario timeout is 60s. The `launch-check.py` script will be implemented separately but reuse patterns from this scenario for cross-referencing evidence."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T09:05:02.361777700+00:00"}}}}
