{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"flax-utensil","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"Wait, the partition wrote 10 rows but mounted 0? That's because `mount_partition` dedupes against `by_id`, and those rows were already in the journal. So \"mounted\" counts *new* rows added, which is 0 here. The gate check should verify the partition file has rows and they're in the ledger, not count new additions. I'll fix the gate check to ensure the partition file exists, has rows, and all its IDs are in the ledger."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T09:06:59.803700200+00:00"}}}}
