{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"_cognition.ai/compaction","params":{"status":"completed","summary":"Full conversation history saved at C:\\Users\\kris_\\AppData\\Roaming\\devin\\cli\\summaries\\history_5117e3e25418418c.md.\nSummary:\n<summary>\n1. Request and Intent:\n\n   The user initiated a build session for development-harness direction-004 in `C:\\builds\\project`. The enduring objective is to create an independent, local-first ecosystem implementation based on `prompt.md`: a persistent assertion ledger, distinct personalities interpreting shared state, configurable tools, local devices/surfaces, useful local agency, reduced provider dependence, lower cost, and user-authorized assistance or automation.\n\n   The user explicitly required a fresh realization in `version 0.3.0.004/`, not a patch or copy of `version 0.3.0.003/`. The previous build must remain intact as a comparison point. GreyAvatar at `C:\\Users\\kris_\\CursorProjects\\GreyAvatar` is reference-only, and prior versions are lineage evidence rather than porting sources.\n\n   Direction-004 is intended to address shortcomings identified in `.003`:\n\n   - G-A/R1: owner-facing controls must actually work through the controls themselves; specifically, the theme selector must restyle the running surface.\n   - G-B/R2: persona voice must constrain register without sacrificing factual fidelity. Persona answers must preserve source facts; unsupported claims must be flagged or withheld rather than invented.\n   - G-C/R3: dyadic confidence is draft guidance and skippable for this run. If implemented, new personalities should start with held confidence `0.5`.\n   - G-D/R4: Library must expose browsable, inspectable holdings—personas, tools, packages, and artifacts—not merely a ledger/log view.\n   - G-E/R5: roster must permit active-personality selection and reordering, with every shipped persona reachable.\n   - G-F/J1–J4: evidence must be clean: no duplicated roster seeding, populated `playbackMs` fields or no such claim, two adequate competing tools, and scenario files embedding check results inline.\n\n   Fleet install and fleet discovery are explicitly deferred and must be honestly declared absent rather than faked. Exchange media is also expected to remain absent at this parity level.\n\n   The user required accessible evidence inside `version 0.3.0.004/` for clean launch and launch hygiene, existing-feature parity against GreyAvatar, completeness, fleet install, exchange media, time-to-readiness-gate, and the full 26-scenario suite. `S-list-project` and `S-personality-create` must be genuinely enacted for enactment credit. The amended scenarios require real selector operation for `S-color-schemes`, selection plus reorder for `S-personality-roster`, and new `S-library-browse` and `S-faithful-voice` scenarios.\n\n   Before stopping, the Cycle 4 entry in `devlog.md` must have its `Result:` and `Time to implement` fields completed, while `Verdict` must remain for a separate judge session.\n\n2. Key Concepts and Values:\n\n   Repository and governing files:\n\n   - Workspace: `C:\\builds\\project`\n   - Required reading order:\n     1. `AGENTS.md`\n     2. `direction-004.md`\n     3. `shortcomings-004.md`\n     4. `prompt.md`\n   - Adopted read-only conventions: `C:\\Project\\MigrateInbound\\CONVENTIONS.md`\n   - Prompt source: `C:\\Project\\MigrateInbound\\ProjectPrompt.md`\n   - Scenario suite: `C:\\builds\\project\\.devin\\scenarios.md`\n   - JEV contract: `C:\\builds\\project\\.devin\\jev-prompt.md`\n   - GreyAvatar capability manifest: `C:\\builds\\project\\.devin\\jev-ref-greyavatar.out`\n   - Cycle log: `C:\\builds\\project\\devlog.md`\n   - Build prompt: `.devin/build-prompt-004.md`\n   - Build ACP log: `.devin/build-cycle-004.acp.log`\n\n   Existing lineage:\n\n   - `version 0.3.0.001/`\n   - `version 0.3.0.002/`\n   - `version 0.3.0.003/`\n   - `.003` was the immediate comparison point and had a Python stdlib implementation with ledger, personas, tools, readiness gate, launch hygiene, UI tabs, and scenario evidence, but failed the live-control, persona-fidelity, Library, and roster-operability bars.\n\n   Application concepts:\n\n   - Append-only assertion ledger as the book of record.\n   - Typed values: string, number, boolean, enum, ref, list, map.\n   - Assertions preserve source/claimant, certainty, contextual confidence, provenance/basis, time, supersession, and relationships.\n   - Claimant vocabulary includes `principal`, `persona:*`, `steward:*`, `model:*`, `source:*`, `surface:*`, `pipeline:*`, `engine:*`, `seed:*`, `tool:*`, `exchange:*`, and `system`.\n   - Basis kinds distinguish captured input, interpretation, source evidence, generated response, execution evidence, user choice, durable result, import, seed, config, and refusal.\n   - Computed views and caches remain subordinate to the ledger.\n   - Needs/templates govern tool work; candidate values remain inspectable until selection.\n   - Personalities are persistent privileged objects outside semantic ledger identity.\n   - Exchange imports must remain below action/acceptance threshold by default.\n   - Consequential effects require witnessed authority/grants.\n   - Speech floor must serialize playback and record real playback durations.\n   - Execution conventions:\n     - `C-TwoPartExecution`\n     - `C-ReadinessGate`\n     - `C-LaunchPartition`\n     - `C-TransientBoundary`\n     - `C-SnapshotInference`\n     - `C-SequentialCommit`\n\n   Environment discovered:\n\n   - Windows environment with Python `3.12.4` at `C:\\Users\\kris_\\AppData\\Local\\Programs\\Python\\Python312\\python.exe`\n   - Ollama at `C:\\Users\\kris_\\AppData\\Local\\Programs\\Ollama\\ollama.exe`\n   - Node at `C:\\Program Files\\nodejs\\node.exe`\n   - Ollama version `0.40.16`\n   - Available models:\n     - `llama3.2:latest` with completion/tools capability\n     - `moondream:latest` with completion/vision capability\n   - Wikipedia API was reachable.\n   - Windows SAPI voices available:\n     - `Microsoft David Desktop`\n     - `Microsoft Zira Desktop`\n\n   Existing `.003` UI and evidence patterns inspected:\n\n   - `version 0.3.0.003/app/ui/index.html` had roster rail, tabs, chat, inbox, command, Library, workshops, exchange, settings, log, status bar, theme selector, and personality editor.\n   - `.003` advertised four themes (`light`, `dark`, `sepia`, `slate`) but the owner found the selector nonfunctional.\n   - `.003` had a display-only roster and did not support active selection/reordering.\n   - `.003` Library was primarily an assertion/log browser rather than holdings inspection.\n   - `.003` scenario driver ran 24 scenarios; direction-004 requires 26.\n\n3. Task Requirements:\n\n   Clarity of task:\n\n   - This is an implementation/build task, not merely a planning or review task.\n   - The entire application must be realized fresh in `version 0.3.0.004/`.\n   - `.003` must not be copied or modified.\n   - GreyAvatar and prior builds may be read for comparison and evidence, but are not code-porting sources.\n   - Fleet installation, fleet discovery, and exchange media must not be faked. Their absence must be declared and counted against completeness.\n\n   Directly stated requirements include:\n\n   - “fresh from prompt”\n   - “Realize the entire application new in `version 0.3.0.004/`; do NOT copy `version 0.3.0.003/`”\n   - “G-A live owner-facing controls, not mechanism-only affordances”\n   - “G-B persona voices as register constraints on truthful output”\n   - “answers preserve the factual content of their sources; unsupported claims flagged or withheld, never invented”\n   - “G-D Library as a library — browsable, inspectable holdings”\n   - “G-E roster as an operable control — select the active personality, reorder entries”\n   - “G-F clean evidence — no double-seeded rosters, populated fields (`playbackMs` or no claim), two adequate competing tools, scenario files carrying their check results inline”\n   - “Fleet install and fleet discovery remain deferred”\n   - “Do not fake the expected-0 criteria.”\n   - “Honesty: report failures honestly — no ok:true-while-failing, no silent stubs, no env-dependent silent degradation.”\n   - “A failed cycle is recorded, not retried.”\n   - “Before stopping: update the Cycle 4 entry in devlog.md — fill the Result: field with what was built, where it lives, and evidence paths, and record the session end in the Time to implement field. Do NOT fill the Verdict; a separate judge session records that.”\n\n   Required implementation areas:\n\n   - Core model and ledger:\n     - JSONL durability\n     - typed assertions\n     - computed/current views\n     - contextual confidence\n     - snapshots\n     - launch partition\n     - transient boundary\n     - compaction\n   - Tools:\n     - registry\n     - DSL\n     - needs/templates\n     - candidate values\n     - grants/authority\n     - built-in tools\n     - two adequate competing tools on the same need\n   - Personas:\n     - persistent storage\n     - minimal creation and later extension\n     - distinct registers\n     - truthful/fidelity guard\n     - unsupported-claim handling\n     - imitation/ethics boundary\n     - unique portrait art\n     - voice configuration\n     - active selection and reorder\n   - Engines/connectors:\n     - live Ollama where available\n     - SAPI speech with actual playback timing\n     - local source connectors\n     - temporal handling\n     - steward\n     - archive\n     - comparison\n     - exchange\n     - readiness gate\n   - API/runtime:\n     - HTTP API\n     - SSE\n     - watchdog\n     - two-part boot\n     - launch hygiene\n     - refusal on an owned port\n     - clean shutdown\n   - UI:\n     - functional theme selector\n     - roster selection/reordering\n     - Library holdings browser and inspector\n     - personality editor\n     - status bar\n     - inbox/context flow\n     - chat/tool invocation\n     - focus and reset controls\n   - Evidence:\n     - launch procedure\n     - fresh launch logs\n     - machine-readable launch report\n     - gate timestamp and duration\n     - scenario transcripts/results for all 26 scenarios\n     - FEATURES manifest with convention conformance/challenges\n     - explicit absent-capability declarations\n     - real outputs, not canned claims\n\n   Testing/verification expectations:\n\n   - Run launch hygiene checks against real processes.\n   - Demonstrate readiness-gate passage and record time-to-gate.\n   - Run the complete scenario driver against a live server.\n   - Canonical scenarios must be actual enactments:\n     - `S-list-project`\n     - `S-personality-create`\n   - `S-color-schemes` must drive the owner-facing selector and observe a restyle.\n   - `S-personality-roster` must exercise selection and reorder.\n   - `S-library-browse` must inspect holdings.\n   - `S-faithful-voice` must verify source-faithful output in register.\n   - Scenario files must include their check results inline.\n   - Evidence must distinguish `enactment` from `repository`.\n   - JEV later emits JSON only and does not modify files; the current build session must not fill the verdict.\n\n   Forbidden actions:\n\n   - Do not copy `.003`.\n   - Do not silently depart from conventions.\n   - Do not claim fleet install/discovery or exchange media if absent.\n   - Do not report `ok:true` while launch or checks fail.\n   - Do not silently degrade when environment-dependent capability is unavailable.\n   - Do not fill the JEV verdict in the build session.\n   - Do not retry a failed cycle automatically.\n\n4. Additional Instructions:\n\n   - The harness skill was invoked at the beginning because this is a development-harness cycle.\n   - The harness process requires coordinator/build/JEV role separation.\n   - `C:\\Project` and `C:\\Harness` are read-only corpora; cite rather than copying wholesale.\n   - Conventions are challengeable but never ignorable. Any departure must identify the convention, departure, reason, and evaluation.\n   - Owner silence is agreement for JEV score fields.\n   - Scenario evidence must not confuse repository evidence with enactment evidence.\n   - The project’s `AGENTS.md` says each cycle realizes the entire application, builds emit accessible evidence, and every cycle entry must be completed before stopping.\n   - The current direction has a one-cycle budget and one approach.\n   - Time-to-gate is a standing scored criterion and must be represented in accessible evidence.\n   - Time-to-implement is tracked but not scored.\n   - No chat rename or preference quiz was used; the assistant inferred reasonable defaults.\n   - Skills/tools were invoked or considered for harness operation, project corpus/conventions, avatar/GreyAvatar relationship, and Windows shell handling.\n\n5. Errors and Fixes:\n\n   - A shell command failed with:\n     `unexpected EOF while looking for matching '\"'`.\n     This was a quoting error while attempting to inspect files. Work continued with corrected commands.\n\n   - Initial attempts to edit `version 0.3.0.004/app/connectors.py` failed because the expected text was not found. The file had CRLF line endings and content differed from the expected patch context. The file was inspected with line-ending-aware commands; subsequent work proceeded without relying on that failed replacement.\n\n   - The file-writing mechanism inserted blank lines after nearly every line in many generated Python files. Compile output showed:\n     - `app/builtins.py`: syntax error at conditional expression around line 141.\n     - `app/floor.py`: unexpected indentation around line 161.\n     - `app/host.py`: unexpected indentation around line 271.\n     - `app/ledger.py`: missing colon around line 288.\n     - `app/personas.py`: invalid syntax around line 688.\n   - The errors were traced to blank lines splitting backslash-continued expressions, for example:\n     - `named = 1.0 if ... or \\` followed by a blank line before the continuation.\n     - Similar split expressions in `floor.py`, `ledger.py`, `host.py`, and `personas.py`.\n   - The generated files were “despaced” by removing empty lines from affected Python files. After this, the compile check reported `COMPILED`.\n   - The same blank-line insertion was observed in the newly written `__main__.py`, UI files, and stylesheets. These were also despaced. The final output reported:\n     - `app/__main__.py`: 165 nonblank lines\n     - `app/ui/app.js`: 526 nonblank lines\n     - `app/ui/index.html`: 174 nonblank lines\n     - `app/ui/styles.css`: 125 nonblank lines\n     - `ALL_COMPILE`\n   - An attempted correction of a malformed `PRELOADS` expression in `api.py` initially failed because the exact malformed string did not match. The API file was ultimately rewritten fully, removing the malformed block.\n   - A malformed intermediate `api.py` contained accidental fragments such as `PREL OADS`; the full rewrite at message 116 corrected the module.\n   - No user feedback about these errors was supplied; the assistant diagnosed and fixed them directly.\n\n6. Problem Solving:\n\n   The assistant first read the required project files, then reviewed the scenario suite, JEV contract, GreyAvatar manifest, conventions, `.003` implementation, UI, scenario driver, and Cycle 4 devlog entry.\n\n   The assistant verified the local environment before implementing engine behavior. It found a live Ollama installation with `llama3.2`, reachable Wikipedia, and SAPI voices, allowing the fresh build to honestly use real local engines rather than silently stubbing them.\n\n   The implementation strategy was to create a new Python stdlib application under `version 0.3.0.004/`, internally named Vantage in some generated source comments/headers, while retaining Meridian-like functionality and direction requirements.\n\n   Files/modules created or substantially written:\n\n   - `version 0.3.0.004/app/__init__.py`\n   - `app/model.py`\n   - `app/ledger.py`\n   - `app/floor.py`\n   - `app/dsl.py`\n   - `app/tools.py`\n   - `app/engines.py`\n   - `app/speechfloor.py`\n   - `app/art.py`\n   - `app/personas.py`\n   - `app/connectors.py`\n   - `app/temporal.py`\n   - `app/archive.py`\n   - `app/compare.py`\n   - `app/setbuild.py`\n   - `app/steward.py`\n   - `app/gate.py`\n   - `app/host.py`\n   - `app/builtins.py`\n   - `app/api.py`\n   - `app/__main__.py`\n   - `app/ui/index.html`\n   - `app/ui/styles.css`\n   - `app/ui/app.js`\n\n   Architectural decisions visible from the work:\n\n   - `model.py` defines typed values, claimant validation, basis kinds, assertion dataclass, IDs, timestamps, and append-only semantics.\n   - `ledger.py` handles JSONL persistence, query/filtering, current versus superseded assertions, snapshots, views, partition state, and compaction.\n   - `floor.py` handles needs/templates, candidate values, requirements, execution, and authority checks.\n   - `personas.py` handles persistence, roster data, personality creation, register metadata, fidelity checks, and persona-specific behavior.\n   - `engines.py` integrates Ollama and local/fallback engine descriptions.\n   - `speechfloor.py` serializes generated speech and records playback metrics.\n   - `art.py` generates identity-bound procedural portrait artifacts.\n   - `connectors.py` includes local source ingestion and source-aware evidence.\n   - `gate.py` records input readiness, ledger readiness, pass timestamp, and time-to-gate.\n   - `host.py` assembles runtime state, handles launch partition/transient state, and coordinates components.\n   - `builtins.py` contains the command/tool registry, chat-turn routing, respondent selection, inference drafts, sequential commits, project/list operations, exchange operations, and built-in workflows.\n   - `api.py` exposes HTTP endpoints, SSE, roster/library/holdings operations, settings, chat, tools, scenario-driving endpoints, and watchdog support.\n   - `__main__.py` is intended to implement Part 1 boot through the