{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"flax-utensil","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"It looks like `generate-portrait` isn't called for API-minted personas, only onboard ones. The docstring implies portraits are bound at minting, and the scenario expects `p[\"art\"]` for all entries. This suggests either minting should generate the portrait directly, or the scenario needs to call onboard for all personas. Binding art at mint seems like the most straightforward way to meet the \"unique portrait art\" requirement. I'll check the `art.generate` and `h_generate_portrait` signatures."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T09:16:36.673187100+00:00"}}}}
