{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"flax-utensil","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm considering how to handle factual queries where no supporting facts are retrieved. Instead of marking them as grounded, I should flag them with `persona:fidelity-flag` set to \"no-source-evidence\" and respond honestly. This requires a minimal change to `serve_response/_reply` in `personas.py` to avoid altering the core `grounded` flag logic."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T09:17:07.182015400+00:00"}}}}
