{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"flax-utensil","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"It seems retrieval failed transiently, or `_facts_for_text` didn't run. The `hits=0` suggests `run-search` also found nothing, meaning either the search need didn't execute or Wikipedia returned empty. Since `_facts_for_text` strips question words to build the query, and I've tested this successfully, a transient failure during the suite run is the most likely cause."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T09:17:13.528808+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"flax-utensil","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm considering how to handle cases where no facts are retrieved. If `grounded=True` by default, unsupported claims might pass checks. A better approach is to explicitly mark fidelity as `{\"grounded\": True, \"unsupported\": True, \"note\": \"no source evidence on record\"}` and flag it, or withhold the answer. Flagging seems more useful. However, I need to ensure my scenario check correctly accounts for these flags, as `all(g is not False)` might still pass if `grounded` remains `True`."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T09:17:15.446665200+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"flax-utensil","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI need to make retrieval more robust. Currently, `_facts_for_text` only records successful source usage, not retrieval attempts. I'll add ledger rows for retrieval attempts, noting success or failure, and ensure the check for \"source evidence retrieved + used\" correctly accounts for actual evidence. Also, I'll address inconsistencies where Wikipedia search might return titles with summaries that fail, and ensure query stripping is handled consistently between search intents and fact extraction."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T09:17:18.434232100+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"flax-utensil","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm considering how to handle factual prompts when no supporting facts are retrieved. The `serve_response` function needs to know if the prompt was factual to correctly flag replies. Passing an `expect_facts` flag from `run_chat_turn` to `serve_response` and then to `_reply` seems like a viable solution to distinguish between casual chats and factual queries that lack evidence."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T09:17:19.426850700+00:00"}}}}
