{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"flax-utensil","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"I've gathered all the necessary changes. The `host.py` fix involves setting the exchange schema and correcting the `root` property to point to the `app` package directory. For `personas.py`, the `mint` function needs to generate and bind art after the ledger persona profile, requiring a specific import and using the `art.generate` signature. The `compose` function in `personas.py` needs an `expect_facts` parameter to handle cases with no source evidence, flagging them appropriately while preserving existing paths when facts are present. I need to verify all callers of `compose`, especially `serve_response`. In `builtins.py`, `_facts_for_text` should record `search:hit` for chat retrievals and add retry logic with `search:adequacy` recording. `serve_response` also needs to pass through the `expect_facts` parameter. Finally, `scenarios.py` has a minor adjustment to `conn.read(8)`."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T09:17:28.833027500+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"flax-utensil","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm refining the evidence recording for the `faithful-voice` scenario. Instead of just checking for `source:retrieval` rows, I'll ensure `_facts_for_text` records `search:hit` on success and `retrieval:attempt` on both success and failure paths, including query, success status, and fact count. The scenario check will then be updated to accept `search:hit` or `source:used` rows, or `retrieval:attempt` rows where the attempt was successful and facts were generated."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T09:17:30.609396300+00:00"}}}}
