{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"flax-utensil","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"Something re-seeded the personas. The `seed_packs` logic seems to prevent this, as it checks for a ledger marker before seeding. However, the `write_partition` and `mount_partition` functions might be involved, though they don't directly mint personas into the store. The only other minting calls are from API requests for Wendell and Marlowe."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T09:22:44.045543+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"flax-utensil","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm questioning whether `rm -rf runtime/scenario` actually succeeded, as a leftover `personalities.json` could explain the double seeding. If `ledger.jsonl` also survived, it would prevent re-seeding, but if only `personalities.json` persisted, it might lead to the observed behavior. Alternatively, `load()` might deduplicate, and `roster()` could be appending to an existing order. I'm also considering if `Ledger.load()` is being called twice, perhaps by separate `Ctx` instances created by the HTTP server or steward. I need to check `gate.run` and `mount_partition` for any unexpected seeding triggers."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T09:22:47.168957500+00:00"}}}}
